  "data": {
    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "06. Other Concepts",
    "ruleNumber": "06.02",
    "summary": "A unit's controlling player resolves each **mortal wound** it suffers 1 at a time, until all are inflicted or the unit is **destroyed**. For each:\n\n1. Select Model: pick by the first choice below that applies.\n2. Resolve Damage: that model loses 1 wound and is destroyed if this leaves it with 0.\n\nThe choices, in order:\n\n- a non-**CHARACTER** model that has lost wounds\n- otherwise any non-**CHARACTER** model\n- otherwise a **CHARACTER** model that has lost wounds\n- otherwise any **CHARACTER** model\n\nNo save is made. If attacks inflict both normal damage and mortal wounds, resolve all the normal damage first. Normal damage comes from the D characteristic of a weapon; mortal wounds an attack inflicts alongside it are part of that attack.",
